					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Tacvi</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>July 28, 2004, 02:25:20 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Any news from Tacvi?&nbsp; Arch Overseers gained access over a month ago and I&#039;ve yet to hear a thing about the zone.&nbsp; Recently someone asked about it on AO&#039;s message board and got one response:<br /><br />&quot;Alcohol. The cause of and solution to, Tacvi.&quot;<br /><br /> :wtf:<br /><br />Is this zone, the final one in GoD, cockblocked too?</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Tacvi</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Stargazeron</b> on <b>July 28, 2004, 03:38:19 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Zone is bugged, it crashes alot.&nbsp; No one has been able to do much of anything there.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Tacvi</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>July 29, 2004, 01:34:59 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">ah ok, so once again we have confirmation that a Sony cockblock (Uqua) was to try to keep people out of unfinished content?&nbsp; Good job, morons at Sony!&nbsp; You&#039;d think they would have learned to finish coding and at least some significant testing of zones before releasing them after that stupid Luclin experience.&nbsp; &quot;Yeah, we figure we&#039;ll finish VT 8 or 10 months after we release the expansion.&nbsp; No one will get there before then.&quot;&nbsp; Then there was the infamous Rathe council cockblock.&nbsp; &quot;Oh noz!&nbsp; We have to finish coding Plane of Time!&quot;&nbsp; <br /><br />Anymore top end guilds quit since Tacvi was entered and found to be a steaming pile of poo?&nbsp;  8)</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Tacvi</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Zerxes</b> on <b>July 29, 2004, 01:56:26 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Pretty good summary of the zone (and GoD to a lesser extent) from yet another satisfied SoE customer:<br /><br />http://fohguild.org/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=12084[/url]<br /><br /><br />And in SoE&#039;s defense (in their attempt to show that they are a *new* company now after the Weekend at Smedley&#039;s), its response:<br /><br />[url]http://eqlive.station.sony.com/community/dev_view.jsp?id=63024<br /><br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Tacvi</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Heloisa</b> on <b>July 29, 2004, 01:58:09 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Well on the bright side OoW is set to launch on Sept 13th     :banghead2:   <br /><br />source : EB games<br /><br /><i>/ponders if WoW will be out by then</i><br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">the Weekend at Smedley&#039;s</div><br /><br />LOL they should make a movie about that.. .opps nm they already did<br /><br /><br />cheers  :wiggle:<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Tacvi</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Gilluian</b> on <b>July 30, 2004, 02:22:17 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">6/13?!!! =(</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Tacvi</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>July 30, 2004, 01:35:04 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Heh... he said September, so 9/13.&nbsp; Hopefully that&#039;s not too soon.&nbsp;  :devil: It probably won&#039;t be finished.<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Tacvi</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Cyquinn</b> on <b>August 01, 2004, 04:25:48 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Why in the name of all that&#039;s holy would you want to finish a game before it ships?&nbsp; :banghead2:&#039;</div>
